 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nRelationships.get_or_add returns wrong relationship\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `get_or_add` method in the Relationships class is returning the wrong relationship when searching for existing relationships. It appears to be matching any relationship regardless of the actual criteria.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx.opc.rel import Relationships\nfrom docx.opc.part import Part\n\n# Create relationships collection\nrels = Relationships()\n\n# Add some relationships with different types and targets\npart1 = Part(...)  # some part\npart2 = Part(...)  # different part\n\nrel1 = rels.get_or_add(\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/hyperlink\", part1)\nrel2 = rels.get_or_add(\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image\", part2)\n\n# This should return rel1, but returns the wrong relationship\nfound_rel = rels.get_or_add(\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/hyperlink\", part1)\n\n# Expected: found_rel should be the same as rel1\n# Actual: found_rel might be rel2 or some other relationship\n```\n\nThe issue seems to affect the relationship matching logic where it's not properly checking the relationship type, target, and external status before determining if a relationship already exists.\n</issue>\n",
